{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And in the morning and you shall see, etc.</b> The meaning of \"morning\" is what He said nearby: ״וַיֹּאמֶר מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ וְהִנֵּה כְבוֹד ה׳״ (Exodus 16:9-10), and this matter occurred on the second day. According to this, the reason for His saying <b>and you shall see</b> with the added vav is — meaning, besides the matter that He will speak to you through me, HaShem will further do for you a thing that will show you His glory. Or it may intend by His saying <b>and in the morning</b> that also in the morning they shall know that HaShem, etc., and it connects above with His saying ״עֶרֶב וִידַעְתֶּם וְגוֹ׳ וּבֹקֶר״, and His saying ״וּרְאִיתֶם״ is the beginning of a new matter; and accordingly it is possible that on that very day they saw the glory of HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:39.979718735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}